   "source": [
    "An elevator controller keeps moving in its current direction (\"up\" or \"down\"), serving every requested floor on the way, \n",
    "then reverses to serve the rest. A request for the current floor is served first, and duplicate requests are served once. \n",
    "Return the floors in the order they are served."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "a971d3e3-82ca-4ea4-aa9b-44648f216690",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "raw"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "Example 1:\n",
    "Input: current = 3, direction = \"up\", requests = [5, 1, 7, 2]\n",
    "Output: [5, 7, 2, 1]\n",
    "Explanation: going up it stops at 5 and 7, then reverses and stops at 2 and 1.\n",
    " \n",
    "Example 2:\n",
    "Input: current = 4, direction = \"down\", requests = [6, 2, 4, 9]\n",
    "Output: [4, 2, 6, 9]\n",
    " \n",
    "Example 3:\n",
    "Input: current = 1, direction = \"down\", requests = [3, 3, 2]\n",
    "Output: [2, 3]\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: don’t forget to commit and push your changes!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "b6574e45-96c1-4304-822a-705e8ce822b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
